## Testing anti-patterns

When writing or editing **tests** (or mocks) in the mobile app, follow **[docs/shared/testing-anti-patterns.md](../../../docs/shared/testing-anti-patterns.md)**.

**Iron laws (short):**

1. **Never** assert mock behavior as if it were product behavior.
2. **Never** add test-only methods to production classes.
3. **Never** mock without knowing the real dependency you are isolating.

**Core principle:** Test what the code **does**, not what the **mocks** do. Prefer accessibility-oriented queries over test IDs when asserting UI.

Cross-reference: **[docs/front-end/tests.md](../../../docs/front-end/tests.md)** · Registry tests: **[dependency-injection.md](../../../docs/front-end/dependency-injection.md)** (clear/register, do not `jest.mock` the Registry module).

